 "notes": [
  "LibreVNA",
  "Supplied through the DC jack J1 (5 V); USB (Q1/Q2) uses the same path. Currents from datasheets (typ.) or estimated. According to the manual the device draws up to 1.2 A at 5 V. LEDs and small parts below 1 mA are not included.",
  "Total at the 5 V input about 5.4 W, 90 % of the manual's maximum (1.2 A at 5 V = 6 W). The temperature estimate treats the board as open in air; the real device sits in a closed aluminium shield, which it does not model (docs/research/thermal.md, section 7.4).",
  "Stackup as in the project's Gerber job file (εr per layer, tanδ 0.02); USB data lines given a class of their own with the USB 2.0 target; the RF class keeps kisi's generic 50 Ω profile on purpose; ferrites BLM15AX601SN1 with the data sheet's DC resistance.",
  "Not filled in (optional): capacitor ratings – no project document gives rated voltage or dielectric (the BOM lists value and package only), so kisi's assumed rating applies; thermal data (PI_THERMAL) of 11 parts – package defaults apply (estimates).",
  "Power tree first converted from a kisi power tree with tools/tree_to_fields.py."
 ],
